# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — Decisions

APPEND-ONLY. This file is never replaced with a new dated copy — every
entry below goes at the bottom, oldest first. If you (the AI working this
codebase) are about to create `decisions-2026-*.md` or similar, stop:
open this file and append instead.

Log an entry here whenever you make a call that isn't obvious from the
diff alone — picking a library, choosing an architecture, rejecting an
alternative, a tradeoff a future session would otherwise have to
re-derive from scratch. Skip routine changes (typo fixes, formatting,
straightforward bug fixes with one obvious solution).

Entry format:

```
## D<n> — <short title> (<date>)

**Decision:** what was chosen.
**Why:** the reasoning — what alternatives existed, what the tradeoff was.
**Alternatives rejected:** what else was considered and why it lost.
```

Before proposing a major change (new dependency, architecture shift,
breaking a public interface), read this file first — the decision may
already be made, or the same alternative may already be rejected.

